  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"x\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"n\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"x\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\"}}],\"questions\":[]}","","","Missing field: fields");
  plans.decode("{\"title\":\"x\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"n\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"x\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[]}}],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","");
  plans.decode("{\"title\":\"x\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"keep\",\"text\":\"Keep\",\"sources\":[\"request\"],\"needs\":[]}],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","");
  let options: selection.Option[] = [{id:"first",criteria:"First"},{id:"second",criteria:"Second"}];
  let issued: selection.Question[] = [selection.question("choice","remaining","coverage","Select",options)];
  let answers: selection.Answer[] = selection.decode("{\"answers\":[{\"id\":\"choice\",\"selected\":\"first\",\"probabilities\":[{\"id\":\"second\",\"p\":0.5},{\"id\":\"first\",\"p\":0.5}]}]}",issued);
  insist(answers[0].accepted && answers[0].selected === "first","Inclusive threshold / issued-order tie");
  let rejected: boolean = false; try { selection.decode("{\"answers\":[{\"id\":\"choice\",\"selected\":\"second\",\"probabilities\":[{\"id\":\"first\",\"p\":0.5},{\"id\":\"second\",\"p\":0.5}]}]}",issued); } catch (error) { rejected = true; } insist(rejected,"Wrong tie winner");
  rejected = false; try { selection.decode("{\"answers\":[{\"id\":\"choice\",\"selected\":\"first\",\"probabilities\":[{\"id\":\"first\",\"p\":1}]}]}",issued); } catch (error) { rejected = true; } insist(rejected,"Missing option");
  rejected = false; try { selection.decode("{\"answers\":[{\"id\":\"choice\",\"selected\":\"first\",\"probabilities\":[{\"id\":\"first\",\"p\":0.66},{\"id\":\"second\",\"p\":0.33}]}]}",issued); } catch (error) { rejected = true; } insist(rejected,"Rounded sum is invalid; never renormalize Jev answers");
  let screen: screens.Screen = screens.reserve(plan,"chat"); insist(screen.target === "chat" && screen.slots[0].status === "open","Need reservation");
  // A composition issues exactly one slot per need and a slot is identified by its need.
  let slotJson: string = "{\"id\":\"remaining\",\"need\":\"remaining\",\"reads\":[],\"writes\":[],\"provider\":false,\"allowedKinds\":[],\"reason\":\"\",\"status\":\"open\"}";
  let duplicateSlots: boolean = false;
  try { screens.decode("{\"screen\":{\"title\":\"Test\",\"target\":\"screen\",\"layout\":{\"kind\":\"stack\"},\"slots\":["+slotJson+","+slotJson+"],\"instances\":[]},\"bindings\":{},\"actions\":{},\"connections\":[]}","screen",["remaining"]); } catch (error) { duplicateSlots = true; }
  insist(duplicateSlots,"Two slots for one need were admitted");
  duplicateSlots = false;
  try { screens.decode("{\"screen\":{\"title\":\"Test\",\"target\":\"screen\",\"layout\":{\"kind\":\"stack\"},\"slots\":[{\"id\":\"alias\",\"need\":\"remaining\",\"reads\":[],\"writes\":[],\"provider\":false,\"allowedKinds\":[],\"reason\":\"\",\"status\":\"open\"}],\"instances\":[]},\"bindings\":{},\"actions\":{},\"connections\":[]}","screen",["remaining"]); } catch (error) { duplicateSlots = true; }
  insist(duplicateSlots,"A slot whose identity differs from its need was admitted");
  insist(screens.catalogueKinds().length === 36,"Catalogue vocabulary");
  let ledger: coverage.Ledger = coverage.judge(plan,screen,[]);
  insist(ledger.needs[0].status === "missing" && ledger.requirements[0].status === "missing","Unimplemented requirement marked covered");
  let independent: plans.Plan = plans.decode("{\"title\":\"Excluded action\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"exclude\",\"text\":\"No booking\",\"sources\":[\"request\"],\"needs\":[]}],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","");
  let emptyScreen: screens.Screen = screens.reserve(independent,"screen");
  let questions: selection.Question[] = coverage.questions(independent,emptyScreen);
  insist(questions.length === 1 && questions[0].id === "requirement_exclude","Original requirement omitted from coverage batch");
  insist(coverage.judge(independent,emptyScreen,[]).requirements[0].status === "unchecked","Missing requirement judgment fabricated coverage");
  let judged: selection.Answer[] = selection.decode("{\"answers\":[{\"id\":\"requirement_exclude\",\"selected\":\"covered\",\"probabilities\":[{\"id\":\"covered\",\"p\":1},{\"id\":\"missing\",\"p\":0}]}]}",questions);
  insist(coverage.judge(independent,emptyScreen,judged).requirements[0].status === "covered","Explicit original exclusion judgment lost");
  let parsed: custom.Parsed = custom.parse("<classes></classes><fields></fields><functions></functions><view>export view Main(state: app.AppState): View { ui.Text(text: state.label) }</view>");
  insist(parsed.accepted,"Full custom fragment regions");
  insist(!custom.parse("<view>x").accepted && !custom.parse("<view>x</view><view>y</view>").accepted,"Malformed/truncated fragment admitted");
  let prerequisites: operations.Prerequisites = {ready:true,unexpired:true,revision:0,lifetime:"session",epoch:1};
  let operation: operations.Operation = operations.begin(operations.idle("load","owner"),"read",prerequisites,{},["call1","call2"],100,200);
  let first: operations.Envelope = operations.envelope(operation,"call1");
  let duplicate: operations.Operation = operations.begin(operation,"other",prerequisites,{},["replacement"],110,210);
  insist(!duplicate.accepted && duplicate.sequence === operation.sequence && duplicate.phase === "read","Pending duplicate mutated invocation");
  insist(operations.sendCurrent(duplicate,first,prerequisites),"Admission marker confused with currentness");
  let completed: operations.Operation = operations.complete(operation,{envelope:first,accepted:true,status:"error",outcome:"failure",message:"Denied"},prerequisites);
  insist(completed.status === "pending","Batch ended before terminal rows");
  let second: operations.Envelope = operations.envelope(completed,"call2");
  completed = operations.complete(completed,{envelope:second,accepted:true,status:"ready",outcome:"success",message:"",result:12},prerequisites);
  insist(completed.status === "error" && completed.outcome === "failure","Last success hid earlier failure");
  let newer: operations.Operation = operations.begin(completed,"read",prerequisites,{},["newcall"],120,220);
  let stale: operations.Operation = operations.complete(newer,{envelope:first,accepted:true,status:"ready",outcome:"success",message:"",result:99},prerequisites);
  insist(stale.status === "pending" && stale.sequence === newer.sequence && !Object.hasOwn(stale,"result"),"Old reply cleared new work");
  let newEnvelope: operations.Envelope = operations.envelope(newer,"newcall");
  let revoked: operations.Prerequisites = {ready:true,unexpired:true,revision:0,lifetime:"session",epoch:2};
  insist(!operations.sendCurrent(newer,newEnvelope,revoked),"Regrant revived old invocation");
  let operands: formula.Operand[] = [{id:"value",expression:"state.value",type:"number",dependency:"f_parts_value"}];
  let expression: formula.Expression = formula.compile("value * 2 + 1",operands);
  insist(expression.dependencies.length === 1 && expression.type === "number","Formula did not retain issued typed dependencies");
  const lazy = formula.compile("choose(true, 7, 1 / 0)",[]); insist((lazy.number as number) === 7 && lazy.source.includes(" ? "),"Lazy choose lowering/value");
  const rounded = formula.compile("round(-0.5)",[]); insist((rounded.number as number) === 0 && 1 / (rounded.number as number) < 0,"round lost negative zero");
  const tied = formula.compile("round(2.5)",[]); insist((tied.number as number) === 3,"Round tie toward positive infinity");
  const negativeTie = formula.compile("round(-1.5)",[]); insist((negativeTie.number as number) === -1,"Round tie at a negative half");
  const belowTie = formula.compile("round(2.4)",[]); insist((belowTie.number as number) === 2,"round below a tie is not a ceiling");
  const extrema = formula.compile("max(min(8, 3), 2)",[]); insist((extrema.number as number) === 3,"min/max formula lowering");
  const precedence: formula.Expression = formula.compile("2 + 3 * 4",[]); insist((precedence.number as number) === 14,"Formula precedence");
  const unaryNumber: formula.Expression = formula.compile("-(2) + 3",[]); insist((unaryNumber.number as number) === 1,"Unary numeric formula");
  const unaryBoolean: formula.Expression = formula.compile("!false",[]); insist((unaryBoolean.boolean as boolean) === true,"Unary boolean formula");
  const booleanPrecedence: formula.Expression = formula.compile("false && true || true",[]); insist((booleanPrecedence.boolean as boolean) === true,"Boolean formula precedence");
  // A boolean operator over issued boolean operands keeps the host operator in the lowered source, so the
  // emitted policy short-circuits the right operand instead of evaluating both eagerly.
  let shortOperands: formula.Operand[] = [{id:"flag",expression:"state.flag",type:"boolean",dependency:"f_parts_flag"},{id:"other",expression:"state.other",type:"boolean",dependency:"f_parts_other"}];
  const shortCircuit: formula.Expression = formula.compile("flag && other",shortOperands);
  insist(strings.contains(shortCircuit.source,"state.flag && state.other"),"Boolean && was not lowered to the short-circuiting host operator: "+shortCircuit.source);
  const shortOr: formula.Expression = formula.compile("flag || other",shortOperands);
  insist(strings.contains(shortOr.source,"state.flag || state.other"),"Boolean || was not lowered to the short-circuiting host operator: "+shortOr.source);
  const comparison: formula.Expression = formula.compile("2 <= 2",[]); insist((comparison.boolean as boolean) === true,"Comparison formula");
  const floored: formula.Expression = formula.compile("floor(1.9)",[]); insist((floored.number as number) === 1,"floor formula");
  const ceiled: formula.Expression = formula.compile("ceil(1.1)",[]); insist((ceiled.number as number) === 2,"ceil formula");
  const absolute: formula.Expression = formula.compile("abs(-2)",[]); insist((absolute.number as number) === 2,"abs formula");
  const squareRoot: formula.Expression = formula.compile("sqrt(9)",[]); insist((squareRoot.number as number) === 3,"sqrt formula");
  const exclusion: formula.Expression = formula.compile("3 !== 3",[]); insist((exclusion.boolean as boolean) === false,"Exclusion formula");
  for (let source of ["value = 4","value[0]","clock.nowMillis()","missing + 1","value && true","1e999"]) {
    let refused: boolean = false; try { formula.compile(source,operands); } catch(error) { refused = true; } insist(refused,"Unsafe formula admitted: "+source);
  }
  let mismatchedBranches: boolean = false; try { formula.compile("choose(true, 1, true)",operands); } catch(error) { mismatchedBranches = true; } insist(mismatchedBranches,"Unsafe formula admitted: choose(true, 1, true)");
  return null;
}
class WireEdit { file:string; search:string; replace:string; }
class EditRequest { revision:string; digest:string; edits:WireEdit[]; }
function editRequest(revision:string,digest:string,edits:WireEdit[]):string { const value:EditRequest = {revision:revision,digest:digest,edits:edits}; return JSON.stringify(value) as string; }
export async function edits(): Promise<null> {
  let fields: embedding.WireField[] = [];
  let textSchema: embedding.WireType = {kind:"string",fields:fields,element:null,maximum:8192,minimumNumber:-1.7976931348623157e308,maximumNumber:1.7976931348623157e308};
  let parameters: embedding.Parameter[] = [{name:"description",type:textSchema}];
  let numberSchema: embedding.WireType = {kind:"number",fields:[],element:null,maximum:128,minimumNumber:-1.7976931348623157e308,maximumNumber:1.7976931348623157e308};
  let functions: embedding.CapabilityFunction[] = [{name:"prepare",description:"Prepare a review, not a purchase",parameters:parameters,result:textSchema},{name:"plan",description:"Plan a review",parameters:[{name:"title",type:textSchema},{name:"count",type:numberSchema}],result:textSchema}];
  let contracts: embedding.CapabilityContract[] = [{module:"host/test",description:"Test review",version:1,functions:functions}];
  let registry: bindings.Registry = bindings.create(contracts);
  let args: Record<string, unknown> = {description:"draft"};
  let rawBinding: Record<string, unknown> = {module:"host/test",function:"prepare",arguments:args};
  await bindings.issueDescriptor(registry,JSON.parse("{\"id\":\"review\",\"label\":\"Prepare\",\"input\":{\"sourceId\":\"draft\",\"label\":\"Description\",\"initial\":\"Specific requirement\"}}"),"prepareReview",rawBinding);
  insist(registry.sources.length === 1 && registry.bindings.length === 1 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Descriptor issuance");
  let rejectedBinding: boolean = false;
  try { bindings.issueBinding(registry,"steal",rawBinding,"anotherDescriptor"); } catch (error) { let failure: Error = error as Error; rejectedBinding = failure.name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA"; }
  insist(rejectedBinding && registry.sources.length === 1 && registry.bindings.length === 1 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Foreign descriptor draft admitted");
  rejectedBinding = false;
  try { await bindings.issueDescriptor(registry,JSON.parse("{\"id\":\"broken\",\"label\":\"Prepare\",\"input\":{\"sourceId\":\"newDraft\",\"label\":\"Description\",\"initial\":\"\"}}"),"brokenBinding",JSON.parse("{\"module\":\"host/test\",\"function\":\"missing\",\"arguments\":{\"description\":\"newDraft\"}}")); } catch (error) { let failure: Error = error as Error; rejectedBinding = failure.name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA"; }
  insist(rejectedBinding && registry.sources.length === 1 && registry.bindings.length === 1 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Failed descriptor partially published");
  // Parameter order follows the frozen contract; a wrong-typed or unissued argument and a duplicate
  // binding or descriptor identity reject before anything is published.
  let countSource: bindings.Source = {id:"count",type:"number",schema:numberSchema,dependencies:[],owner:"review",payloadOwner:"review",getter:"count",ready:"ready_count"};
  bindings.reserve(registry,countSource);
  let orderedArguments: Record<string, unknown> = {count:"count",title:"draft"};
  let orderedBinding: Record<string, unknown> = {module:"host/test",function:"plan",arguments:orderedArguments};
  bindings.issueBinding(registry,"planReview",orderedBinding,"review");
  insist(bindings.binding(registry,"planReview").parameterOrder.join(",") === "title,count","Binding parameter order");
  let duplicateBinding: boolean = false;
  try { bindings.issueBinding(registry,"planReview",orderedBinding,"review"); } catch (error) { let failure: Error = error as Error; duplicateBinding = failure.name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA"; }
  insist(duplicateBinding,"Duplicate binding identity admitted");
  insist(registry.sources.length === 2 && registry.bindings.length === 2 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Duplicate binding rejection published partial state");
  let wrongArguments: Record<string, unknown> = {description:"count"};
  let wrongBinding: Record<string, unknown> = {module:"host/test",function:"prepare",arguments:wrongArguments};
  let wrongArgument: boolean = false;
  try { bindings.issueBinding(registry,"wrongArgument",wrongBinding,"review"); } catch (error) { let failure: Error = error as Error; wrongArgument = failure.name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA"; }
  insist(wrongArgument,"Wrong-typed binding argument admitted");
  insist(registry.sources.length === 2 && registry.bindings.length === 2 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Wrong-typed binding rejection published partial state");
  let unissuedArguments: Record<string, unknown> = {description:"absent"};
  let unissuedBinding: Record<string, unknown> = {module:"host/test",function:"prepare",arguments:unissuedArguments};
  let unissuedArgument: boolean = false;
  try { bindings.issueBinding(registry,"unissuedArgument",unissuedBinding,"review"); } catch (error) { let failure: Error = error as Error; unissuedArgument = failure.name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA"; }
  insist(unissuedArgument,"Unissued binding argument source admitted");
  insist(registry.sources.length === 2 && registry.bindings.length === 2 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Unissued binding rejection published partial state");
  let duplicateDescriptor: boolean = false;
  try { await bindings.issueDescriptor(registry,JSON.parse("{\"id\":\"review\",\"label\":\"Again\",\"input\":{\"sourceId\":\"otherDraft\",\"label\":\"Description\",\"initial\":\"\"}}"),"anotherBinding",JSON.parse("{\"module\":\"host/test\",\"function\":\"prepare\",\"arguments\":{\"description\":\"otherDraft\"}}")); } catch (error) { let failure: Error = error as Error; duplicateDescriptor = failure.name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA"; }
  insist(duplicateDescriptor,"Duplicate descriptor identity admitted");
  insist(registry.sources.length === 2 && registry.bindings.length === 2 && registry.actions.length === 1,"Duplicate descriptor rejection published partial state");
  let base: revisions.Revision = await revisions.issue({deal:"alpha alphaEnd β",dealui:"view Ω"});
  let rejected: revisions.Applied = await revisions.apply(base,editRequest(base.revision,base.digest,[{file:"deal",search:"alpha",replace:"x"}]));
  insist(!rejected.accepted && rejected.current.revision === base.revision,"Ambiguous edit modified revision");
  rejected = await revisions.apply(base,editRequest("forged",base.digest,[{file:"deal",search:"β",replace:"x"}])); insist(!rejected.accepted,"Unissued revision");
  rejected = await revisions.apply(base,editRequest(base.revision,base.digest,[{file:"deal",search:"alphaEnd β",replace:"x"},{file:"deal",search:"β",replace:"y"}])); insist(!rejected.accepted,"Overlapping edits");
  let applied: revisions.Applied = await revisions.apply(base,editRequest(base.revision,base.digest,[{file:"deal",search:"alphaEnd",replace:"z"},{file:"deal",search:"β",replace:"😀"},{file:"dealui",search:"Ω",replace:"δ"}]));
  insist(applied.accepted && applied.current.source.deal === "alpha z 😀" && applied.current.source.dealui === "view δ","Atomic source pair");
  insist(applied.current.revision !== base.revision && applied.current.digest !== base.digest,"Fresh issued identity");
  let operation: inference.Operation = inference.operation("section",2);
  let failed: boolean = false; try { await inference.ask(operation,"custom","","","",6000,false); } catch (error) { failed = true; }
  insist(failed && operation.used === 1,"Failure not charged");
  await inference.ask(operation,"custom","","","",6000,false);
  failed = false; try { await inference.ask(operation,"custom","","","",18000,true); } catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; failed = error.name === "ASK_LIMIT"; }
  insist(failed && operation.used === 2,"Nested cap dispatch");
  return null;
}
export async function planningLimits(): Promise<null> {
  let input: planning.Input = {requestId:"request",request:"Preserve all constraints",facts:"{}",factIds:[],sourceIds:[],contracts:"[]",specification:"Plan contract",target:"screen"};
  let result: planning.Result = await planning.run(input);
  insist(result.plan !== null && result.asks === 3,"Planning retry/escalation bounds");
  let reviewed: planning.Result = await planning.review(input,result);
  insist(reviewed.asks === 3,"Empty question batch dispatched");
  result = await planning.run(input);
  insist(result.plan === null && result.asks === 3,"Failed planning exceeded cap or fabricated plan");
  return null;
}
// ---- Action triggers are a second-batch decision -------------------------------------------
function action(id: string, on: string, at: string): string {
  let source: string = ""; if (at !== "") { source = ",\"at\":\""+at+"\""; }
  return "{\"id\":\""+id+"\",\"type\":\"action\",\"words\":\"Perform "+id+"\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"on\":\""+on+"\""+source+",\"operation\":\"host/ops.run\"}}";
}
function triggerPlan(): plans.Plan {
  return plans.decode("{\"title\":\"Triggers\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"when\",\"label\":\"When\",\"kind\":\"time\",\"measure\":\"minutes\",\"value\":600},{\"id\":\"length\",\"label\":\"Length\",\"kind\":\"count\",\"measure\":\"seconds\",\"value\":90}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":["
    +"{\"id\":\"timer\",\"type\":\"countdown\",\"words\":\"Count down\",\"reads\":[\"length\"],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Timer\",\"length\":\"length\"}},"
    +"{\"id\":\"rows\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log rows\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Rows\",\"fields\":[]}},"
    +action("ends","countdown_end","timer")+","
    +action("taps","row_tap","rows")+","
    +action("clocked","time","when")+","
    +action("tapped","button","")+","
    +action("later","other","")+","
    +action("lost","other","")+"],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","");
}
function ids(needs: plans.Need[]): string[] { let result: string[] = []; for (let need of needs) { result[result.length] = need.id; } return result; }
function answer(id: string, selected: string, p: number): selection.Answer { return {id:id,selected:selected,probability:p,accepted:p >= selection.threshold("ordinary"),probabilities:[{id:selected,p:1},{id:"unavailable",p:0}]}; }
function optionIds(question: selection.Question): string[] { let result: string[] = []; for (let option of question.options) { result[result.length] = option.id; } return result; }
export function triggers(): null {
  let plan: plans.Plan = triggerPlan();
  insist(ids(events.unsettled(plan)).join(",") === "later,lost","Only unresolved triggers stay open: "+ids(events.unsettled(plan)).join(","));
  let issued: selection.Question[] = events.questions(plan);
  insist(issued.length === 2 && issued[0].id === "events_later" && issued[1].id === "events_lost","One events question per unsettled action");
  insist(issued[0].decision === "ordinary" && issued[0].threshold === 0.25,"Events question copies the ordinary threshold");
  // Only `button` (without a source) and the triggers whose source resolves in the plan are offered.
  insist(optionIds(issued[0]).join(",") === "button,countdown_end_timer,entry_added_rows,row_tap_rows,time_when,unavailable","Issued trigger alternatives: "+optionIds(issued[0]).join(","));
  // A clock is a `countdown_end` source, never the `time` source a scheduled action names.
  insist(!s.contains(optionIds(issued[0]),"time_timer"),"A countdown was offered as a time source");
  // An entry trigger naming a source the plan never issues rejects at decode, so the question is
  // only ever asked over sources that resolve; the issued tap stays legal and is offered.
  let absent: string = "";
  try { plans.decode("{\"title\":\"Triggers\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"rows\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log rows\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Rows\",\"fields\":[]}},"+action("missing","entry_added","absent")+"],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"",""); }
  catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; absent = error.message; }
  insist(absent === "missing: unissued trigger target absent","Unissued entry trigger target: "+absent);
  let lost: string[] = optionIds(issued[1]); insist(s.contains(lost,"row_tap_rows") && !s.contains(lost,"entry_added_absent"),"Eligibility of issued sources: "+lost.join(","));
  // Settling binds the chosen trigger on the plan itself, so the writer receives it and no later
  // batch re-asks it.
  let settled: events.Settlement = events.settle(plan,[answer("events_later","button",1),answer("events_lost","row_tap_rows",1)]);
  insist(settled.settled.join(",") === "later,lost","Settled trigger identities");
  insist(events.questions(plan).length === 0,"Settled trigger re-asked");
  let later: plans.Need = plan.needs[6]; let lostNeed: plans.Need = plan.needs[7];
  insist((later.spec.on as string) === "button" && !Object.hasOwn(later.spec,"at"),"Button trigger must omit its source");
  insist((lostNeed.spec.on as string) === "row_tap" && (lostNeed.spec.at as string) === "rows","Chosen trigger source not bound");
  // `other`/unavailable keeps the trigger with the written action and never invents one.
  let custom: plans.Plan = triggerPlan();
  let kept: events.Settlement = events.settle(custom,[answer("events_later","unavailable",1),answer("events_lost","unavailable",1)]);
  insist(kept.settled.length === 0 && kept.outcomes.length === 2,"Unavailable trigger settled a source");
  insist((custom.needs[6].spec.on as string) === "other" && !Object.hasOwn(custom.needs[6].spec,"at"),"Unavailable trigger rewrote the plan");
  insist(kept.outcomes[0].status === "custom" && kept.outcomes[0].reason.includes("declare its trigger"),"Custom trigger reason");
  // Unanswered and below-threshold answers leave the need visibly open with a located reason.
  let unanswered: events.Settlement = events.settle(triggerPlan(),[]);
  insist(unanswered.outcomes.length === 2 && unanswered.outcomes[0].status === "open" && unanswered.outcomes[0].reason.includes("unanswered"),"Unanswered trigger not reported");
  let below: events.Settlement = events.settle(triggerPlan(),[{id:"events_later",selected:"button",probability:0.1,accepted:0.1 >= selection.threshold("ordinary"),probabilities:[]},{id:"events_lost",selected:"button",probability:0.1,accepted:0.1 >= selection.threshold("ordinary"),probabilities:[]}]);
  insist(below.outcomes[0].status === "open" && below.outcomes[0].reason.includes("threshold"),"Below-threshold trigger not reported");
  // The located reason reaches the composition as a visibly missing slot, so no later stage can
  // claim the need and no writer is told to implement an inferred trigger.
  let reserved: screens.Screen = screens.reserve(triggerPlan(),"screen");
  events.apply(reserved,events.settle(triggerPlan(),[]));
  let marked: number = 0;
  for (let slot of reserved.slots) { if (slot.need === "later" || slot.need === "lost") { marked = marked+1; insist(slot.status === "missing" && slot.reason.includes("Unsettled action trigger"),"Unsettled trigger slot: "+slot.need+" "+slot.status); } }
  insist(marked === 2,"Unsettled trigger slots: "+s.encode(marked));
  let written: screens.Screen = screens.reserve(triggerPlan(),"screen");
  events.apply(written,events.settle(triggerPlan(),[answer("events_later","unavailable",1),answer("events_lost","unavailable",1)]));
  let left: number = 0;
  for (let slot of written.slots) { if (slot.need === "later" || slot.need === "lost") { left = left+1; insist(slot.status === "open" && slot.reason === "Implementation not selected","Custom trigger slot was closed: "+slot.need+" "+slot.status); } }
  insist(left === 2,"Custom trigger slots: "+s.encode(left));
  // Ineligible issued alternatives reject: an unissued trigger and a button that carries a source.
  let unissued: string = "";
  try { events.settle(triggerPlan(),[answer("events_later","countdown_end_when",1),answer("events_lost","button",1)]); }
  catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; unissued = error.message; }
  insist(unissued.includes("Ineligible issued trigger alternative"),"Unissued trigger alternative admitted: "+unissued);
  let carrying: string = "";
  try { events.settle(triggerPlan(),[answer("events_later","button_when",1),answer("events_lost","button",1)]); }
  catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; carrying = error.message; }
  insist(carrying.includes("Ineligible issued trigger alternative"),"Button alternative carrying a source admitted: "+carrying);
  // A trigger whose named source the plan does not resolve is never offered, and a decoded plan that
  // carries a non-identifier source rejects instead of raising an unclassified host type error.
  let nontext: string = "";
  try { events.unsettled(plans.decode("{\"title\":\"x\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"act\",\"type\":\"action\",\"words\":\"Act\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"on\":\"other\",\"at\":7,\"operation\":\"host/ops.run\"}}],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","")); }
  catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; nontext = error.name+":"+error.message; }
  insist(nontext === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA:need act.at: expected text","Non-text trigger source: "+nontext);
  return null;
}
// ---- Human question review closes every proposed question exactly once -----------------------
function humanQuestion(id: string): string { return "{\"id\":\""+id+"\",\"text\":\"Which option?\",\"default\":\"a\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"label\":\"A\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"label\":\"B\"}]}"; }
function questionPlan(questions: string): plans.Plan { return plans.decode("{\"title\":\"Pick\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"preserve\",\"text\":\"Keep the request\",\"sources\":[\"request\"],\"needs\":[]}],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"body\",\"type\":\"other\",\"words\":\"Something useful\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{}}],\"questions\":["+questions+"]}",[],[],"",""); }
function seeded(plan: plans.Plan, closed: string[]): planning.Result { return {plan:plan,diagnostics:"",answers:[],asks:0,review:[],closed:closed}; }
function reviewInput(requestId: string): planning.Input { return {requestId:requestId,request:"Keep the request",facts:"{}",factIds:[],sourceIds:[],contracts:"[]",specification:"Plan contract",target:"screen"}; }
export async function reviewAdmission(): Promise<null> {
  // 0.59 does not reach the human-question threshold of 0.6: nothing is shown, the issued default
  // stands and the decision is retained with its winning probability.
  let low: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-low"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[]));
  insist(low.review.length === 1 && !low.review[0].admitted && low.review[0].probability === 0.59 && low.review[0].threshold === 0.6,"Below-threshold review admission");
  insist((low.answers[0].optionId as string) === "a" && (low.plan as plans.Plan).questions.length === 1,"Unadmitted question lost its default");
  insist(low.closed.join(",") === "q1","Unadmitted question was not closed");
  // Exactly 0.6 admits; an unanswered host reply uses the issued default and performs no replan.
  let at: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-at"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[]));
  insist(at.review[0].admitted && at.asks === 1,"Inclusive human-question threshold");
  insist((at.answers[0].optionId as string) === "a" && (at.plan as plans.Plan).questions.length === 1,"Default-only resolution changed the plan");
  // A nondefault option answer triggers exactly one answered replan that preserves requirement ids
  // and clears the question list.
  let changed: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-changed"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[]));
  insist(changed.asks === 2 && changed.review[0].probability === 0.75,"One answered replan expected");
  // The replan reply proposes its own question, so only the answered-replan path can clear it.
  insist((changed.plan as plans.Plan).questions.length === 0 && (changed.plan as plans.Plan).requirements[0].id === "preserve","Answered replan did not close the question");
  insist((changed.answers[0].optionId as string) === "b" && changed.closed.join(",") === "q1","Answer trace lost");
  // A winning `default` admits nothing whatever its probability.
  let byDefault: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-default"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[]));
  insist(!byDefault.review[0].admitted && byDefault.review[0].selected === "default" && (byDefault.answers[0].optionId as string) === "a","Winning default admitted a question");
  // A refused, absent or malformed review admits nothing, keeps every default and raises no error.
  let unusable: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-unusable"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[]));
  insist(!unusable.review[0].admitted && (unusable.answers[0].optionId as string) === "a" && unusable.asks === 1,"Unusable review raised or admitted");
  // Three admissible proposed questions show the first two in plan order; the third takes its
  // issued default without error and is closed all the same.
  let three: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-three"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")+","+humanQuestion("q2")+","+humanQuestion("q3")),[]));
  insist(three.review.length === 3 && three.review[0].admitted && three.review[1].admitted && !three.review[2].admitted,"Third admissible question was shown");
  insist(three.closed.join(",") === "q1,q2,q3" && (three.answers[0].id as string) === "q3" && (three.answers[0].optionId as string) === "a","Third question was not defaulted and closed");
  insist((three.answers[1].id as string) === "q1" && (three.answers[2].id as string) === "q2","Shown questions lost their plan order");
  // Free text is bounded in UTF-16 units: 4096 is accepted exactly and triggers the answered replan.
  let long: planning.Result = await planning.review(reviewInput("request-long"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[]));
  insist((long.answers[0].text as string).length === 4096 && long.asks === 2,"Accepted free text length lost");
  // 4097 units, blank text, both answer kinds and an unissued option each reject with their
  // located reason and authorize no source repair.
  for (let kind of ["overlong","blank","both","unissued"]) {
    let rejected: string = "";
    try { await planning.review(reviewInput("request-"+kind),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[])); }
    catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; rejected = error.name+":"+error.message; }
    let expected: string = kind === "overlong" || kind === "blank" ? "Question text length" : kind === "both" ? "Option and text are mutually exclusive" : "Unissued question option";
    insist(rejected === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA:"+expected,"Rejected question answer: "+kind+" -> "+rejected);
  }
  // A question already closed by this request rejects instead of being asked twice.
  let reissue: string = "";
  try { await planning.review(reviewInput("request-at"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),["q1"])); }
  catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; reissue = error.name+":"+error.message; }
  insist(reissue === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA:Question already closed: q1","Closed question reissue: "+reissue);
  // Cancellation ends generation with the cancellation classification.
  let cancelled: boolean = false;
  try { await planning.review(reviewInput("request-cancel"),seeded(questionPlan(humanQuestion("q1")),[])); } catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; cancelled = error.name === "CANCELLED"; }
  insist(cancelled,"Cancelled question did not end generation");
  return null;
}
function figurePlan(decimals: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"limit\",\"label\":\"Limit\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":10}],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"total\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"words\":\"Total\",\"reads\":[\"limit\"],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Total\",\"format\":\"money\",\"unit\":\"EUR\",\"formula\":\"limit\",\"decimals\":"+decimals+",\"example\":{\"inputs\":{\"limit\":10},\"result\":10}}}]}"; }
function yesNoPlan(result: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"over\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"words\":\"Over\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Over\",\"format\":\"yes_no\",\"unit\":\"\",\"formula\":\"true\",\"example\":{\"inputs\":{},\"result\":"+result+"}}}]}"; }
function entriesPlan(fieldDecimals: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"log\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"amount\",\"label\":\"Amount\",\"kind\":\"number\",\"initial\":0,\"measure\":\"number\",\"decimals\":"+fieldDecimals+"},{\"id\":\"what\",\"label\":\"What\",\"kind\":\"text\",\"initial\":\"\",\"measure\":\"number\",\"decimals\":"+fieldDecimals+"}]}}]}"; }
function textEntriesPlan(fieldDecimals: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"log\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log\",\"reads\":[],\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"what\",\"label\":\"What\",\"kind\":\"text\",\"initial\":\"\",\"measure\":\"number\",\"decimals\":"+fieldDecimals+"}]}}]}"; }
function seedPlan(seeds: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"log\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log\",\"reads\":[],\"quote\":\"I bought coffee\",\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"what\",\"label\":\"What\",\"kind\":\"text\",\"initial\":\"\",\"measure\":\"number\"},{\"id\":\"done\",\"label\":\"Done\",\"kind\":\"toggle\",\"initial\":false,\"measure\":\"number\"},{\"id\":\"amount\",\"label\":\"Amount\",\"kind\":\"number\",\"initial\":0,\"measure\":\"number\"}],\"seeds\":["+seeds+"]}}]}"; }
function emptyEntriesPlan(seeds: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"log\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log\",\"reads\":[],\"quote\":\"I bought coffee\",\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[],\"seeds\":["+seeds+"]}}]}"; }
function textSeedPlan(seeds: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"log\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log\",\"reads\":[],\"quote\":\"I bought coffee\",\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"what\",\"label\":\"What\",\"kind\":\"text\",\"initial\":\"\",\"measure\":\"number\"}],\"seeds\":["+seeds+"]}}]}"; }
function toggleSeedPlan(seeds: string): string { return "{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"questions\":[],\"needs\":[{\"id\":\"log\",\"type\":\"entries\",\"words\":\"Log\",\"reads\":[],\"quote\":\"I bought coffee\",\"spec\":{\"label\":\"Log\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"done\",\"label\":\"Done\",\"kind\":\"toggle\",\"initial\":false,\"measure\":\"number\"}],\"seeds\":["+seeds+"]}}]}"; }
function operandIds(count: number): formula.Operand[] {
  let issued: formula.Operand[] = []; let index: number = 0;
  while (index < count) { let id: string = "op"+String(index); issued[issued.length] = {id:id,expression:"(state."+id+" as number)",type:"number",dependency:"f_parts_"+id}; index = index+1; }
  return issued;
}
function aggregateIds(count: number): string[] { let issued: string[] = []; let index: number = 0; while (index < count) { issued[issued.length] = "count_"+String(index); index = index+1; } return issued; }
export function planValues(): null {
  // The planner document enters construction as JSON text, so the boundary classifies its own parse:
  // a fenced, truncated or prose-wrapped reply rejects with the construction classification and a
  // located reason the bounded re-plan consumes, never an unclassified host parser error.
  for (let malformed of ["```json\n{\"title\":\"t\"}\n```","{\"title\":","","not json","null","[]","123"]) {
    let name: string = ""; let message: string = "";
    try { plans.decode(malformed,[],[],"",""); }
    catch (errorUnknown) { let error: Error = errorUnknown as Error; name = error.name; message = error.message; }
    insist(name === "CONSTRUCTION_SCHEMA","Unclassified plan document rejection: "+name+" "+message);
    insist(strings.contains(message,"plan:"),"Plan document rejection is not located: "+message);
  }
  refusesPlan("```json\n{\"title\":\"t\"}\n```","","","plan: not a JSON document");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":","","","plan: not a JSON document");
  // A declared kind is checked, never cast, and the rejection names the offending identifier.
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"note\",\"label\":\"Note\",\"kind\":\"text\",\"measure\":\"number\",\"value\":7}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input note: expected text");
  // A numeric kind fed a string is refused at its own identifier instead of being cast.
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"spent\",\"label\":\"Spent\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":\"12\"}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input spent: expected a finite number");
  // The matching percent, amount and bounded amount values still decode with their declared kinds.
  let declaredKinds: plans.Plan = plans.decode("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"ratio\",\"label\":\"Ratio\",\"kind\":\"percent\",\"measure\":\"percent\",\"value\":0.5},{\"id\":\"spent\",\"label\":\"Spent\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":12},{\"id\":\"cap\",\"label\":\"Cap\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":15,\"min\":10,\"max\":20}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","");
  insist(s.finite(declaredKinds.inputs[0].value) === 0.5,"Percent input value lost");
  insist(s.finite(declaredKinds.inputs[1].value) === 12,"Amount input value lost");
  insist(s.finite(declaredKinds.inputs[2].value) === 15 && (declaredKinds.inputs[2].min as number) === 10 && (declaredKinds.inputs[2].max as number) === 20,"Bounded amount input inside its declared bounds was refused");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"flag\",\"label\":\"Flag\",\"kind\":\"toggle\",\"measure\":\"number\",\"value\":\"yes\"}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input flag: expected a boolean");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"items\",\"label\":\"Items\",\"kind\":\"count\",\"measure\":\"count\",\"value\":1.5,\"min\":0,\"max\":9}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input items: expected an integral number");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"items\",\"label\":\"Items\",\"kind\":\"count\",\"measure\":\"count\",\"value\":2,\"min\":0.5,\"max\":9}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input items.min: expected an integral number");
  // Omission means unbounded, not zero: an unbounded count stays valid.
  let unbounded: plans.Plan = plans.decode("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"items\",\"label\":\"Items\",\"kind\":\"count\",\"measure\":\"count\",\"value\":3}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}",[],[],"","");
  insist(!Object.hasOwn(unbounded.inputs[0],"min") && !Object.hasOwn(unbounded.inputs[0],"max"),"Unbounded count gained a bound");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"pick\",\"label\":\"Pick\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"measure\":\"number\",\"value\":3,\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"label\":\"A\",\"value\":1}]}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input pick: choice index outside its options");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"limit\",\"label\":\"Limit\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":4,\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"label\":\"A\",\"value\":1}]}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","options on a non-choice input");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"limit\",\"label\":\"Limit\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":4,\"min\":9}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input limit: value below its minimum");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"limit\",\"label\":\"Limit\",\"kind\":\"amount\",\"measure\":\"money\",\"value\":9,\"max\":4}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input limit: value above its maximum");
  // A wrong-typed declared value rejects with the identifier that carries it. The wire classes declare
  // these as unknown so the located helper decides, instead of the contextual JSON decode rejecting
  // first with a bare "expected boolean/number/array" the planner cannot attribute.
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"items\",\"label\":\"Items\",\"kind\":\"count\",\"measure\":\"count\",\"value\":2,\"setting\":\"yes\"}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input items.setting");
  refusesPlan("{\"title\":\"t\",\"inputs\":[{\"id\":\"items\",\"label\":\"Items\",\"kind\":\"count\",\"measure\":\"count\",\"value\":2,\"unit\":7}],\"constants\":[],\"requirements\":[],\"needs\":[],\"questions\":[]}","","","input items.unit");
